{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>עלות עלי.</b> The flocks and cattle — they are עָלוֹת — are laid upon me to lead them slowly." "<b>עלות.</b> Nursing their young — the language of עוֹלֵל וְיוֹנֵק (Lamentations 2), עוּל יָמִים (Isaiah 65), and שְׁתֵּי פָרוֹת עָלוֹת (I Samuel 6) — and in לַעַז אנפנטיי״ש." "<b>ודפקום יום אחד.</b> To weary them on the road by running <b>and all the flock would die.</b>" "<b>ודפקום.</b> Like קוֹל דּוֹדִי דּוֹפֵק (Song of Songs) — knocking at the door."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French enfanteis, 'nursing mothers'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:56.725023242Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}